   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 618 of the laws of 1998, amending the general\nmunicipal law and the education law relating to disposal of surplus computer\nequipment by political subdivisions, in relation to the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S8338",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8338-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Chap 618 of 1998",
    "lawSection": "General Municipal",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8338\n\nSPONSOR: GAUGHRAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 618 of the laws of 1998, amending the general\nmunicipal law and the education law relating to disposal of surplus\ncomputer equipment by political subdivisions, in relation to the effec-\ntiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to provide a three year extension of chapter\n618 of the laws of 1998, as amended by chapter 60 of the laws of 2019,\nrelating to disposal of surplus computer equipment by political subdivi-\nsions.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill extends chapter 618 of the laws of 1998, as amended by chapter\n60 of the laws of 2019, for three years until July 1, 2025.\n\n \nDIFFERENCE BETWEEN ORIGINAL AND AMENDED VERSION (IF APPLICABLE):\n\nn/a\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe enactment of chapter 618 of the laws of 1998 and the extensions\ngranted enabled political subdivisions to donate surplus computer equip-\nment through SED's C.R.E.A.T.E. Programs (§ 318 of education law). To\ndate, hundreds of computers have been donated to local schools,\nlibraries and other not-for-profit organizations. This bill will extend\nthis law and allow local governments to continue to dispose of surplus\ncomputer equipment in a fair and equitable manner.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019: A6665/S5409 (Otis/MARTINEZ) signed 7/3/19, ch. 60\n\n2016: A10022/S7869 (Otis/MARTINEZ) signed 6/30/16 ch. 79\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately and shall expire July 1, 2025\nwhen upon such date the provisions of this act shall be deemed repealed.\n",
